  "description": "TASK-7 deterministic call-resolution precision baseline. Manifest is the sole baseline update point. Each language draws positive (correct CALLS resolution) and negative (must-not-resolve-elsewhere) evidence from existing resolver fixtures without inventing semantics. Precision = truePositives / (truePositives + falsePositives). falseNegatives counts expected edges that produced zero matching CALLS edges (a miss); missing resolution is never counted as a false positive and never enters the precision denominator. A case with expectFilePath=null is an expected-unresolved case that passes only when no matching CALLS edge exists. Languages with a `parser` field are gated on optional/native grammars: when the grammar is unavailable at runtime the suite records an explicit skipped outcome rather than silently omitting the language. baseline (top-level) is the full-availability aggregate (sum of every per-language baseline); the runtime aggregate is asserted over whichever parser-gated languages are available.",
  "matching": "exact-targetFilePath",
  "skipGraphPhases": true,
